nodecode-membase is a rewrite of unibaseio's unibaseio/membase:

  https://github.com/unibaseio/membase
  commit 8733b537da62192aa088e65ed127340969e0f680
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Unibase (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the Hermes memory provider at `integrations/hermes` — its
three tools (`membase_search`, `membase_save`, `membase_profile`), the
time-boxed, fail-open search before each turn, the opt-in capture of the
operator's own words, and the sentences it explains a refusal with — as Common
Lisp against Membase's HTTP API, the same three endpoints the plugin reaches
through its SDK (`/v1/search`, `/v1/memories/add`, `/v1/profile-facts`). What
was left out: Hermes's own provider registration and per-profile JSON settings
file (the cell declares one config section instead), the `memory.user_store`
hand-over of USER.md facts to the Membase profile, and the SDK's Memory listing
and document upload, which the plugin never exposes to the model either.
